<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; color: #12324F">Anti-wrinkle</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">Helps improve the appearance of wrinkles.</p>
</div>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 12px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; font-size: 14px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-weight: 700; color: #56626D">Active ingredient</p>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">Adenosine</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 24px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; color: #12324F">Key ingredients</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: #56626D">These are the ingredients shown on the front of the package. They are listed separately from the functional ingredients above (ingredients designated for functional cosmetics).</p>
</div>
<p style="margin: 0; border-left: 3px solid #56626D; padding: 4px 0 4px 12px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; color: #56626D">The ‘What research shows’ notes below summarize research on each raw material. They are not tests of NEUVELIF products, and the concentrations and formulations used in the studies differ from this product. This product's efficacy is the UV protection, brightening, and anti-wrinkle functions above.</p>
<div style="background: #12324F; color: #FFFFFF; padding: clamp(22px, 2.5vw, 32px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: #8FD3F2">KEY INGREDIENTS</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700">EGF · IGF · FGF</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: #C9D6E2">Peptide ingredients modeled on protein signaling molecules (growth factors) also found in our own skin.</p>
</div>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(240px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 20px 28px">
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #36506A; padding-top: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; line-height: 1; color: #FFFFFF">EGF</p>
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: #8FD3F2">Epidermal Growth Factor</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #FFFFFF">Epidermal growth factor</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #C9D6E2">A peptide ingredient modeled on a growth factor associated with cells of the epidermis, the skin's outer layer.</p>
<div style="background: #18405F; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #8FD3F2">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #E3ECF3">One study reported improvements in the appearance of fine lines, skin texture, pores, and pigmented spots in 29 women (aged 39–75) who applied a serum containing EGF twice daily for 3 months.</p>
<a href="https://jddonline.com/articles/dermatology/S1545961612P0613X" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #A9BACB; text-underline-offset: 3px">Schouest JM et al., Journal of Drugs in Dermatology, 2012 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #36506A; padding-top: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; line-height: 1; color: #FFFFFF">IGF</p>
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: #8FD3F2">Insulin-like Growth Factor</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #FFFFFF">Insulin-like growth factor</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #C9D6E2">A peptide ingredient modeled on a growth factor structurally similar to insulin.</p>
<div style="background: #18405F; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #8FD3F2">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #E3ECF3">In skin-aging research, it is described as a growth factor involved in cell growth and division. There are still few studies of it applied to human skin as a cosmetic.</p>
<a href="https://www.thieme-connect.de/products/ejournals/html/10.1055/s-0034-1372423" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #A9BACB; text-underline-offset: 3px">Fabi S·Sundaram H, Facial Plastic Surgery, 2014 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #36506A; padding-top: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; line-height: 1; color: #FFFFFF">FGF</p>
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: #8FD3F2">Fibroblast Growth Factor</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #FFFFFF">Fibroblast growth factor</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #C9D6E2">A peptide ingredient modeled on a growth factor associated with fibroblasts, the cells that make collagen in the dermis.</p>
<div style="background: #18405F; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #8FD3F2">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #E3ECF3">In skin-aging research, it is described as a growth factor involved in fibroblast activity and the production of a skin structural protein (fibronectin).</p>
<a href="https://www.thieme-connect.de/products/ejournals/html/10.1055/s-0034-1372423" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #A9BACB; text-underline-offset: 3px">Fabi S·Sundaram H, Facial Plastic Surgery, 2014 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; color: #A9BACB">Research on cosmetics that apply growth factors to the skin is ongoing, but the level of evidence has been assessed as still moderate (Fabi & Sundaram, 2014).</p>
</div>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(260px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 12px">
<div style="border: 1px solid #D5E0E8; border-top: 3px solid #12324F; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #56626D">PANTHENOL</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: #12324F">Panthenol</p>

<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">A precursor of vitamin B5 (provitamin B5).</p>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #1170AE">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">An ingredient widely studied for moisturization and the skin barrier. A review summarizes its moisturizing and barrier-improving effects, including a study in which applying panthenol cream twice daily for 7 days to irritated skin improved skin hydration and barrier function indicators.</p>
<a href="https://informahealthcare.com/doi/abs/10.1080/09546634.2017.1325310" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #56626D; text-underline-offset: 3px">Proksch E et al., Journal of Dermatological Treatment, 2017 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="border: 1px solid #D5E0E8; border-top: 3px solid #12324F; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #56626D">NIACINAMIDE</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: #12324F">Niacinamide</p>
<span style="display: inline-flex; align-self: flex-start; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid #1170AE; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: #1170AE">This product's brightening functional ingredient</span>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">A form of vitamin B3.</p>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #1170AE">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">Its mechanism of reducing the transfer of melanin to the skin's surface cells has been identified, and in a human study with a 5% niacinamide moisturizer, pigmentation decreased and skin became brighter within 4 weeks.</p>
<a href="https://academic.oup.com/bjd/article/147/1/20/6628642" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #56626D; text-underline-offset: 3px">Hakozaki T et al., British Journal of Dermatology, 2002 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
<div style="border: 1px solid #D5E0E8; border-top: 3px solid #12324F; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<p lang="en" style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Noto Sans KR', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #56626D">LILIUM CANDIDUM FLOWER EXTRACT</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; color: #12324F">Madonna lily flower extract</p>

<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">An extract from the flowers of the white lily (Madonna lily), the ingredient behind the product name ‘Backhap’ (Korean for white lily).</p>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #D5E0E8; padding-top: 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #1170AE">What research shows</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3C4752">The flower has long been used in folk remedies and cosmetics in many regions, and several plant compounds in it, such as kaempferol, are known for their antioxidant activity. This product contains 0.001 ppm as an ingredient that symbolizes its name.</p>
<a href="https://www.mdpi.com/2223-7747/9/8/959" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #56626D; text-underline-offset: 3px">Zaccai M et al., Plants, 2020 <svg aria-hidden="true" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex: none"><path d="M7 17L17 7"></path><path d="M8 7h9v9"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

