<div style="flex: 999 1 560px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; border-top: 2px solid #12324F">
<div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">Is it a chemical or a mineral sunscreen?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">It is a chemical (organic) sunscreen. It contains four UV filters: Diethylamino Hydroxybenzoyl Hexyl Benzoate, Ethylhexyl Triazone, Methylene Bis-Benzotriazolyl Tetramethylbutylphenol, and Diethylhexyl Butamido Triazone.</p>
</div>
<div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">Is it a functional cosmetic?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">Yes. It was reported to Korea's Ministry of Food and Drug Safety (MFDS) in June 2025 as a triple-function cosmetic for UV protection, brightening, and wrinkle improvement. The brightening ingredient is niacinamide and the anti-wrinkle ingredient is adenosine.</p>
</div>
<div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">Does it sting the eyes?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">How much you feel it varies from person to person. After 21 women who usually experience eye stinging from cosmetics used it for 2 weeks, their eye stinging score fell by 80.27%. If it gets directly into your eyes, rinse with water.</p>
</div>
<div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">Can people with sensitive skin use it?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">In a 24-hour patch test (34 participants) it scored 0.00 for skin irritation and was classified as non-irritating. Skin reactions vary, though, so try it first on a small area such as behind the ear or along the jawline. If you notice any problem, stop using it and consult a dermatologist.</p>
</div>
<div style="padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D5E0E8; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; color: #12324F">My dermatologist told me to use a mineral sunscreen. Can I use this?</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; color: #3C4752">Please follow your doctor's advice. NEUVELIF Backhap Recovery Sunscreen uses chemical (organic) filters. Some clinics recommend a mineral sunscreen for a while after procedures that leave tiny channels in the skin.</p>
</div>
